[{:db/id "q-89768/selection/c3952568ef2ee93ee3814ca5e82f48a8b13c69d3043e3206a6a213d0e439202c" :answer/id #uuid "d9ecabb7-93b2-50b8-af3f-06d91b6d9bee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=9\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89768/selection/0b7a3541ed5d0497bd178374758f1bb03fb8a56ab2c6c5d25269c61bf30abb03" :answer/id #uuid "0d756cb5-6205-50b4-9906-1773121f4181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=9\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89768/selection/7ee374bde9ff5da74e40d6761be8757cdcadf65482a1c2a737865c173d0f34d8" :answer/id #uuid "5b7644ce-84a8-50f6-abcf-155eb4c75093" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=6\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89768/selection/32ce4237bfda749f1bb2ba92f7d0a08ebe6f2a2f0edc19609a178d0619965beb" :answer/id #uuid "bd90b2ee-e5a1-55cd-baab-6cfa555b27d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89768/selection/11a406866f7f589b6469e0bf8817ea6a35838acd701d117357032ebdc6b73a71" :answer/id #uuid "e2fb28a3-30b3-585a-ac2a-da68e3518dba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=7\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=6\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89768/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ec82df7-cd38-5ee8-b925-b8a85fac3bb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89768/selection/7ee374bde9ff5da74e40d6761be8757cdcadf65482a1c2a737865c173d0f34d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-89768/selection/c3952568ef2ee93ee3814ca5e82f48a8b13c69d3043e3206a6a213d0e439202c" "q-89768/selection/0b7a3541ed5d0497bd178374758f1bb03fb8a56ab2c6c5d25269c61bf30abb03" "q-89768/selection/7ee374bde9ff5da74e40d6761be8757cdcadf65482a1c2a737865c173d0f34d8" "q-89768/selection/32ce4237bfda749f1bb2ba92f7d0a08ebe6f2a2f0edc19609a178d0619965beb" "q-89768/selection/11a406866f7f589b6469e0bf8817ea6a35838acd701d117357032ebdc6b73a71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89768" :question/id #uuid "a8a0ddc8-972a-5f01-829a-2b6930d2f171" :question/math-academy-id "q-89768" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068362/assets/432f8963425031983284db54310c8ae604bc993de66494dceb48e6a4e2bcdf73.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{7}{6}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,-7)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=7.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{7}{6}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{7}{6} \\\\ \\frac{7}{b} & =\\frac{7}{6} \\\\ b & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-89768/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e538c21e-67fd-56f7-b09f-a9fec3121f78"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89768"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-89774/selection/eda6696a18f7e0f4340c36035a2e5ccf4f4a18e3fe0d731385e5fea2ead9cd37" :answer/id #uuid "db033769-6d7e-5417-b27f-49279bb7b70c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89774/selection/bb549ca08eb4f929cdea9d53671ee514828412946f0d93957f3e02e7ab99517e" :answer/id #uuid "2c2031c0-4714-58b5-a884-790c330852b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89774/selection/ecd234c39814c6b7c15a362cd988d1dd43cda774efd90b02f0067e76ffd526fa" :answer/id #uuid "8d5e176a-5c1f-5418-9ad6-89bc3ec7de53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89774/selection/eeef18dce6bbf586dc3710f383787395085ce9419e3e3691567b399a9b6c8011" :answer/id #uuid "40b62951-4ea5-5183-bf6e-bb1af026a536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89774/selection/98fae13bbd3b0c144faed74f886ae7a5deaaba8889210edb94fa851881281c0d" :answer/id #uuid "86890b6b-a375-5288-80c1-558cf05a16f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89774/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce62ac01-b4cc-582a-90f0-d5878cb421c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89774/selection/bb549ca08eb4f929cdea9d53671ee514828412946f0d93957f3e02e7ab99517e" :answer-field/choices ["q-89774/selection/eda6696a18f7e0f4340c36035a2e5ccf4f4a18e3fe0d731385e5fea2ead9cd37" "q-89774/selection/bb549ca08eb4f929cdea9d53671ee514828412946f0d93957f3e02e7ab99517e" "q-89774/selection/ecd234c39814c6b7c15a362cd988d1dd43cda774efd90b02f0067e76ffd526fa" "q-89774/selection/eeef18dce6bbf586dc3710f383787395085ce9419e3e3691567b399a9b6c8011" "q-89774/selection/98fae13bbd3b0c144faed74f886ae7a5deaaba8889210edb94fa851881281c0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89774" :question/id #uuid "e45c70e0-74a6-58a6-9db9-63d038c10666" :question/math-academy-id "q-89774" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068362/assets/245037d572c2bc9c81d3cdfb7a485b167c15223c68e3dbb8e40eaa2cc7650da9.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm x.$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,-1)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=1.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{b} & =1 \\\\ b & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-89774/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e538c21e-67fd-56f7-b09f-a9fec3121f78"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89774"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106623/selection/04ef8157e32d6af582e65c886da8abf4a0c3aebff0c21dc51d7c63a6fe6049df" :answer/id #uuid "dccf38bb-e173-596a-a5e6-40e2594426b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106623/selection/c80fa966185e233ba87c6962829a845d65ff5210e9e28bdac6abecca3b3edf99" :answer/id #uuid "7a8705fc-991a-530c-a9e0-d45dc8ea6831" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106623/selection/51360456424422c7319ad71215d3cd2a01be2d133af9b58170a8436c1ffbdb7c" :answer/id #uuid "a80e0f67-361c-5a78-886b-0c8034ed8c0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106623/selection/3c3a2422729e8f6e4970d71ae012fd4cb1e2a604de9d671c1687bee806aa3a17" :answer/id #uuid "9c2b9737-4208-54a4-9641-00ec2aed40cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106623/selection/8ac95b8754250f7f3dfb9a3cd1c95eb72e8d3b0ad77b30a71ec5e7de3f72faeb" :answer/id #uuid "a62cfca6-edc1-51c2-865e-f477b4e6129c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106623/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "39104662-f3eb-59ae-b338-4ddf553f285d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106623/selection/8ac95b8754250f7f3dfb9a3cd1c95eb72e8d3b0ad77b30a71ec5e7de3f72faeb" :answer-field/choices ["q-106623/selection/04ef8157e32d6af582e65c886da8abf4a0c3aebff0c21dc51d7c63a6fe6049df" "q-106623/selection/c80fa966185e233ba87c6962829a845d65ff5210e9e28bdac6abecca3b3edf99" "q-106623/selection/51360456424422c7319ad71215d3cd2a01be2d133af9b58170a8436c1ffbdb7c" "q-106623/selection/3c3a2422729e8f6e4970d71ae012fd4cb1e2a604de9d671c1687bee806aa3a17" "q-106623/selection/8ac95b8754250f7f3dfb9a3cd1c95eb72e8d3b0ad77b30a71ec5e7de3f72faeb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106623" :question/id #uuid "aa5fba2b-b9cd-5f9f-94be-1d958a9dbda2" :question/math-academy-id "q-106623" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent Identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{5}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+1 & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106623/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "494f9793-de3b-5a0e-8ee9-38a8bad0f970"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106623"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106685/selection/f0096b0075fd1383c2cbc9da986e37d68fe4debee9de7673f7b88ba85761ab71" :answer/id #uuid "4764fa15-f1ec-529c-b513-ed3ac74da8ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106685/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" :answer/id #uuid "e6e2d190-586a-5283-a92b-ca666e36d4a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106685/selection/348a8b4a7fcf2d1c58c5b8fab2d0a6884e7c60f9ed36a3d77e436e84fd15dc7e" :answer/id #uuid "40b74dce-1d22-59f8-8e8f-0eb11a7da9c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106685/selection/b85ba2ba54d596653a563476b4f78775ae06d7693e7e2bfe7b1bde461b8c1155" :answer/id #uuid "524aff31-cbe2-5d1f-bc59-77a837d8d7c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cup (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106685/selection/45cd2b735740b382dba8c4a9519aef5f8524ea3401f4c7f61b59893918513571" :answer/id #uuid "b876ae21-e4ff-57da-a25c-af8d22e1a520" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [0,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106685/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f14aa825-c4f3-5e54-9cd2-d57d683c2d15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106685/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" :answer-field/choices ["q-106685/selection/f0096b0075fd1383c2cbc9da986e37d68fe4debee9de7673f7b88ba85761ab71" "q-106685/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" "q-106685/selection/348a8b4a7fcf2d1c58c5b8fab2d0a6884e7c60f9ed36a3d77e436e84fd15dc7e" "q-106685/selection/b85ba2ba54d596653a563476b4f78775ae06d7693e7e2bfe7b1bde461b8c1155" "q-106685/selection/45cd2b735740b382dba8c4a9519aef5f8524ea3401f4c7f61b59893918513571"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106685" :question/id #uuid "4002f7a8-11ca-5268-8529-2e1c2c8cfac5" :question/math-academy-id "q-106685" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068362/assets/32375f839dd0f51a8624bebda732d7413130c940045db7e5a1a9fce3576e91b6.png)\n\nOne branch of a hyperbola (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a single branch, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068362/assets/d44195c764b2943c3d5b5e0d91ee770011c951d7a825f0c5cc4d1f38cedbb709.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the upper branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the upper branch are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106685/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0dfdda62-1838-540f-bf4d-960353fc3706"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106685"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106687/selection/348a8b4a7fcf2d1c58c5b8fab2d0a6884e7c60f9ed36a3d77e436e84fd15dc7e" :answer/id #uuid "5e7a1b71-fc81-5788-8fb2-bac3e38283bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106687/selection/f0096b0075fd1383c2cbc9da986e37d68fe4debee9de7673f7b88ba85761ab71" :answer/id #uuid "4e1cf1d2-8c03-578f-be36-af20697303b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106687/selection/45cd2b735740b382dba8c4a9519aef5f8524ea3401f4c7f61b59893918513571" :answer/id #uuid "cdf8bf47-2c56-53ce-8177-0d9d7e78d12b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [0,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106687/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" :answer/id #uuid "57897eda-42bc-5dba-b320-d8a3d9ba2188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106687/selection/b85ba2ba54d596653a563476b4f78775ae06d7693e7e2bfe7b1bde461b8c1155" :answer/id #uuid "38248df6-45d9-5619-a06e-bc2bfaeec2e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cup (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106687/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3bdd91e-1ea6-5d0a-be55-5e94695fd3c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106687/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" :answer-field/choices ["q-106687/selection/348a8b4a7fcf2d1c58c5b8fab2d0a6884e7c60f9ed36a3d77e436e84fd15dc7e" "q-106687/selection/f0096b0075fd1383c2cbc9da986e37d68fe4debee9de7673f7b88ba85761ab71" "q-106687/selection/45cd2b735740b382dba8c4a9519aef5f8524ea3401f4c7f61b59893918513571" "q-106687/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" "q-106687/selection/b85ba2ba54d596653a563476b4f78775ae06d7693e7e2bfe7b1bde461b8c1155"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106687" :question/id #uuid "6469c7a5-493e-5e62-84eb-8c3dac67cf01" :question/math-academy-id "q-106687" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068362/assets/1474fb8efcada2aec61c1aa2b2ed16615e0ba968ec4e53a8fbfe05b1107c085f.png)\n\nOne branch of a hyperbola (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a single branch, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068362/assets/46c9d9139a3cff2a76871c69deeac60492d2c9aef4bf1f7ac07a16868d31d6e0.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the upper branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the upper branch are\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106687/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0dfdda62-1838-540f-bf4d-960353fc3706"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106687"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
